      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;setting-up-visual-studio-code-for-p5js&#34;&gt;&#xA;  Setting up Visual Studio Code for p5js&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;heading-link&#34; href=&#34;#setting-up-visual-studio-code-for-p5js&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-link&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; title=&#34;Link to heading&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;sr-only&#34;&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I have always been a great fan of &lt;a href=&#34;https://processing.org/de/&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Processing&lt;/a&gt;, the Java-based language for creative coding. While I do like programming in &lt;code&gt;Python&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;c++&lt;/code&gt; much more than &lt;code&gt;Java&lt;/code&gt;, it is just nice to open the IDE of &lt;code&gt;processing&lt;/code&gt; and start getting creative without setting up complicated frameworks. &lt;a href=&#34;https://p5js.org/&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;p5js&lt;/a&gt; is like &lt;em&gt;Processing&lt;/em&gt; but based on &lt;em&gt;Javascript&lt;/em&gt;, and so the &lt;em&gt;sketches&lt;/em&gt; can be easily shared without other external dependencies.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
